5. Conveying Non-Source Forms.

You may convey a covered work in object code form under the terms
of sections 4 and 5, provided that you also convey the
machine-readable Corresponding Source under the terms of this License,
in one of these ways:

a) Convey the object code in, or embodied in, a physical product
(including a physical distribution medium), accompanied by a
fixed written offer, valid for at least 10 years and valid for as
long as you offer spare parts or customer service for that product,
to give anyone who possesses a copy of the object code a chance to
obtain the complete Corresponding Source in one of the ways
specified in this License, at no charge.

b) Convey the object code in, or embodied in, a physical product
(including a physical distribution medium), accompanied by a
written offer, valid for at least 10 years and valid for as long as
you offer spare parts or customer service for that product, to
give anyone who possesses a copy of the object code a chance to
obtain the complete Corresponding Source from a network server,
at no charge.

c) Convey individual copies of the object code with a copy of the
written offer to provide the Corresponding Source in a network
server, at no charge, valid for at least 10 years and valid for as
long as you offer spare parts or customer service for that product.

d) Convey the object code by offering access from a designated
place (gratis or for a charge), and offer equivalent access to the
Corresponding Source in the same way through the same place at no
charge.

e) Convey the object code using peer-to-peer networks, provided
you inform other peers where the Corresponding Source and the
object code are being offered to the public at no charge.

6. User Products and Consumer Rights.

A "User Product" is either (1) a "consumer product", which means any
tangible personal property that is normally used for personal, family,
or household purposes, or (2) anything designed or sold for
incorporation into a dwelling. "Installation Information" for a User
Product means any methods, procedures, authorization codes, or other
information required to install and run modified versions of a
covered work in that User Product from a modified version of its
Corresponding Source. The installation information must be sufficient
to allow someone to install and run a modified version of the covered
work from a modified version of its Corresponding Source.

